###############################################################################
# NOTES & INSTRUCTIONS
###############################################################################
#
# API v1 ENDPOINTS:
# ✨ Health check: GET /api/v1/health
# ✨ System status: GET /api/v1/status
# ✨ Platform list: GET /api/v1/platforms
# ✨ Single platform: POST /api/v1/platforms/:platform/profiles
# ✨ Aggregate profiles: POST /api/v1/profiles/aggregate
# ✨ API documentation: GET /
#
# SUPPORTED PLATFORMS:
# - leetcode, codeforces, codechef, geeksforgeeks, hackerrank, github
#
# SETUP:
# 1. Update the @variables at the top with real usernames
# 2. Ensure server is running: npm start
# 3. Check .env file for required tokens:
#    - GITHUB_TOKEN (required for GitHub API)
#    - CODECHEF_COOKIE (optional, for better reliability)
#
# USAGE:
# - Click "Send Request" above each ### section
# - Or use keyboard shortcut (Ctrl/Cmd + Alt + R in VS Code)
# - Run tests in order or individually
# - Use REST Client extension for VS Code for best experience
#
# ENDPOINT STRUCTURE:
# - Health endpoints: /api/v1/health, /api/v1/status
# - Platform list: /api/v1/platforms (GET)
# - Single platform: /api/v1/platforms/{platform}/profiles (POST)
# - Aggregate: /api/v1/profiles/aggregate (POST)
#
# EXPECTED BEHAVIOR:
# - Health checks should return instantly (< 100ms)
# - Individual platforms: 1-5 seconds (varies by platform)
# - Aggregate endpoint: 5-15 seconds (all platforms in parallel)
# - GitHub is typically fastest (< 1 second with token)
# - GeeksforGeeks and CodeChef may be slower (3-5 seconds)
#
# ERROR RESPONSES:
# - 400: Bad Request (missing username or invalid platform)
# - 404: Not Found (invalid endpoint)
# - 500: Internal Server Error (platform error or network issue)
#
# RATE LIMITS:
# - GitHub: 5000 req/hour with token, 60 without
# - Other platforms: Vary by platform, space out requests if needed
# - Aggregate endpoint counts as 1 request per platform
#
# TIPS:
# - Use GET /api/v1/platforms to see all supported platforms
# - Use GET /api/v1/status to check server health and memory usage
# - Check logs/ directory for detailed request logs
# - All requests are logged automatically (see logs/error-*.log)
#
###############################################################################
